WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.040
England, 1290.

2
00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:05.490
The king expels every Jewish
person from the country.

3
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.310
Three centuries later, a Jewish
moneylender walks onto a London stage.

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.740
On stage, he tells the hero
what he has put up with:

5
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:19.040
"And spet upon my Jewish gaberdine," So
does the play share its first audience's

6
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.110
prejudice?

7
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.970
Or does it show it up?

8
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.300
In this mission, you'll uncover
the history behind the play,

9
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:29.720
from 1290 to a notorious
court case in 1594.

10
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:32.590
You'll look hard at how the
Christians treat Shylock,

11
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.050
and what they call him.

12
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.240
And you'll follow the play
on stage from 1741 to today,

13
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:40.260
as its audiences change.

14
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:43.970
Your mission: decide whether
the play is antisemitic,

15
00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.900
or about antisemitism.
